            "explanation_html": "<section class=\"dtos-explanation\" aria-label=\"DTOS trade assessment\"><h3>DTOS trade assessment</h3><p class=\"tw-final-verdict\">WORTH PURSUING</p><section class=\"tw-decision\" aria-label=\"Trade decision summary\"><section class=\"tw-decision-lead\" aria-label=\"Decision and next step\"><p>Why this decision: The supported production gain is material; the recorded roster and depth costs still matter.</p><p>Next step: Preview the exact offer, review both teams\u2019 costs and confirm the other manager\u2019s motivation.</p></section><section class=\"tw-decision-market\" aria-label=\"Current Market comparison\"><h4>Current Market</h4><div class=\"tw-market-caption\"><span>You send <b>290</b></span><span>You receive <b>400</b></span></div><div class=\"tw-market-bar\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"You receive 110 more current Market value.\"><span class=\"disadvantage\" style=\"flex-basis:42.029%\"></span><span class=\"advantage\" style=\"flex-basis:57.971%\"></span></div><p>You receive 110 more current Market value.</p><small>Current values, not trade-date grades. Market advantage is separate from strategy and lineup impact.</small></section><p>Conditional current-week optimal legal-lineup gain (Season 2026, week 2): 10.00 projected points. This prepared comparison does not establish dependable availability or replacement cover; review the roster limitations.</p><p>Optimal legal-lineup production improves 10.00 points per supported week. Addresses supported WR lineup/depth context; package effects remain separate. Provisional: check dates and player availability.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Cost and uncertainty: Reserve coverage declines in supported weeks; Useful legal-replacement production falls 13.00 points per supported week</p><p>Your team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change +10.00 projected points.</p><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: +10.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 290 sent / 400 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Useful replacement production changes -13.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 18.00 points (supported, 2 covered reserve slots); after 5.00 points (supported, 1 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: -13.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p>Their team: Conditional Season 2026, week 2 optimal-lineup change +2.00 projected points.</p><p>Conditional average across supported weeks 2, 3, 4, 5: +2.00 projected points per week; not a season forecast.</p><p>Neutral Market: 400 sent / 290 received; this is value compensation, not acceptance evidence.</p><p>Useful replacement production changes -5.00 points per supported week.</p><p>Season 2026, week 2 reserve cover: before 17.00 points (supported, 2 covered reserve slots); after 12.00 points (supported, 2 covered reserve slots).</p><p>Conditional week 2 reserve-production change: -5.00 points; not an injury forecast or a second starting lineup.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Player availability is uncertain; usable replacement production is provisional.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Projection source freshness is qualified; these are conditional projections, not guaranteed production.</p><p>Week 2 \u00b7 Before and after: Original projection observations are not confirmed Fresh; replacement production remains conditional.</p><p>Other weekly reserve effects and coverage gaps are listed separately in Before and after \u00b7 both optimal lineups.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Their recorded direction is RETOOL; it does not prove willingness to accept this offer.</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Market fairness and receiving a pick do not establish rebuilding intent or predict acceptance.</p><p>Review both teams\u2019 sacrifices and discuss the stated compensation and direction with the other manager; this is not a prediction of acceptance.</p><p>Other team: Supported counterparty effects; not a prediction of manager behavior.</p><p>Their cost and uncertainty: Market overpay of 110 units; Useful legal-replacement production falls 5.00 points per supported week</p><p class=\"tw-drawback\">Evidence limit: Incoming availability: 2w \u00b7 Unsigned Projection evidence is Unavailable; retained numerical evidence is provisional, not freshly verified.</p><p>Inspect the main drawback, edit or reevaluate this trade.</p><details class=\"tw-player-facts\"><summary>Player production, projections and rank definitions</summary><section><h4>1qb</h4><p>QB \u00b7 NFL team unavailable \u00b7 Age 23.0 \u00b7 Unknown</p><p>Listed position eligibility: QB. Availability and roster rules are assessed separately in the legal lineup.</p><p>Market positional rank: QB8 \u00b7 Priced rostered players in the selected league.</p><p>Current Market: 145.</p><p>Sleeper projection: 14.00 \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Week 2 \u00b7 Unavailable.</p><p>Sleeper actual production: Unavailable points per completed-week score observation \u00b7 Unknown observations \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Selected league. This is not a games-played average.</p><p>Season fantasy-points rank / points-per-game rank: unavailable; no complete compatible cohort is prepared.</p><details><summary>Player fact sources and coverage</summary><p>Projection source observation: Unknown; source generation: de4d132d9c1d6005313c313b3539513b6c797e07b5486f3be5ad7ccc20311a7d.</p><p>Unavailable</p><p>Actual production source: Unavailable; league league-1; generation Unavailable; observation Unknown.</p><p>Compatible prepared actual production is unavailable; no zero or season rank is inferred.</p></details></section><section><h4>1wb</h4><p>WR \u00b7 NFL team unavailable \u00b7 Age 22.0 \u00b7 Unknown</p><p>Listed position eligibility: WR. Availability and roster rules are assessed separately in the legal lineup.</p><p>Market positional rank: WR8 \u00b7 Priced rostered players in the selected league.</p><p>Current Market: 145.</p><p>Sleeper projection: 4.00 \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Week 2 \u00b7 Unavailable.</p><p>Sleeper actual production: Unavailable points per completed-week score observation \u00b7 Unknown observations \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Selected league. This is not a games-played average.</p><p>Season fantasy-points rank / points-per-game rank: unavailable; no complete compatible cohort is prepared.</p><details><summary>Player fact sources and coverage</summary><p>Projection source observation: Unknown; source generation: de4d132d9c1d6005313c313b3539513b6c797e07b5486f3be5ad7ccc20311a7d.</p><p>Unavailable</p><p>Actual production source: Unavailable; league league-1; generation Unavailable; observation Unknown.</p><p>Compatible prepared actual production is unavailable; no zero or season rank is inferred.</p></details></section><section><h4>2w</h4><p>WR \u00b7 NFL team unavailable \u00b7 Age 29.0 \u00b7 Unknown</p><p>Listed position eligibility: WR. Availability and roster rules are assessed separately in the legal lineup.</p><p>Market positional rank: WR2 \u00b7 Priced rostered players in the selected league.</p><p>Current Market: 400.</p><p>Sleeper projection: 15.00 \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Week 2 \u00b7 Unavailable.</p><p>Sleeper actual production: Unavailable points per completed-week score observation \u00b7 Unknown observations \u00b7 Season 2026 \u00b7 Selected league. This