 they may consider it: The evaluation identifies a supported benefit for their team.</li></ul><h4>Evidence confidence</h4><ul><li>Support for bounded Market/lineup conclusions; not acceptance probability or outcome certainty.</li></ul><details><summary style=\"min-height:44px;cursor:pointer;overflow-wrap:anywhere\">Supporting evidence and limitations</summary><h4>Key evidence</h4><ul><li>Your-side assessment: <strong>WORTH PURSUING</strong> <span>(DTOS interpretation)</span></li><li>Final bilateral qualification: <strong>WORTH PURSUING</strong> <span>(DTOS interpretation)</span></li><li>Accepted recommendation reason: <strong>The supported production gain is material; the recorded roster and depth costs still matter.</strong> <span>(DTOS interpretation)</span></li><li>Your package roster context: <strong>Package optimal lineup: 25 \u2192 35 Sleeper-projected points. Replacement support is recalculated after all player movements. Projection evidence is Unavailable; retained numerical evidence is provisional, not freshly verified. Post-trade availability is uncertain: 1q (unsigned), 1w (unsigned), 2w (unsigned); lineup impact is provisional, not dependable cover.</strong> <span>(DTOS-derived evidence)</span></li><li>QB replacement context: <strong>QB: strategic strength. Player count alone does not establish expendability; review removal effects and reserve assignments. Projection evidence is Unavailable; retained numerical evidence is provisional, not freshly verified. Availability is uncertain for named rostered players; numerical scenarios are provisional, not verified active cover. Under RETOOL, compare sustainable quality and capital costs separately. Availability-qualified post-package starter/reserve counts: 1/0.</strong> <span>(DTOS-derived evidence)</span></li><li>RB replacement context: <strong>RB: not required by lineup. Player count alone does not establish expendability; review removal effects and reserve assignments. Projection evidence is Unavailable; r